Where every file in this directory came from, fetched 2026-09-14.

The woff2 files are the official Google Fonts builds, served by fonts.gstatic.com
in answer to the Google Fonts CSS API request below (a desktop Chrome user agent,
which is what makes it answer with woff2). They are the variable fonts, clipped
to the weight range 400-600, one file per script subset. Nothing was modified.

  https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:wght@400..600&family=Inter:wght@400..600&family=Noto+Serif+Telugu:wght@400..600&family=Noto+Sans+Telugu:wght@400..600&family=Noto+Serif+Devanagari:wght@400..600&family=Noto+Sans+Devanagari:wght@400..600&display=swap

  Fraunces-latin.woff2                 fraunces/v38            subset: latin
  Fraunces-latin-ext.woff2             fraunces/v38            subset: latin-ext (carries the rupee sign's range)
  Inter-latin.woff2                    inter/v20               subset: latin
  Inter-latin-ext.woff2                inter/v20               subset: latin-ext
  NotoSansTelugu-telugu.woff2          notosanstelugu/v30      subset: telugu
  NotoSerifTelugu-telugu.woff2         notoseriftelugu/v29     subset: telugu
  NotoSansDevanagari-devanagari.woff2  notosansdevanagari/v30  subset: devanagari
  NotoSerifDevanagari-devanagari.woff2 notoserifdevanagari/v34 subset: devanagari

The licences are the OFL.txt files from the google/fonts repository, main branch:

  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/fonts/main/ofl/<family>/OFL.txt

All six families are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, which permits
bundling and self-hosting. The licence text must travel with the fonts, which is
why it is here and not only linked.

SHA256SUMS covers every font and licence file; scripts/check-site.py verifies it.
To refresh: repeat the request above, replace the files, regenerate SHA256SUMS
(shasum -a 256 *.woff2 *.txt > SHA256SUMS) and update the versions in this file.
